CSharpAuthor 2.0 migration patch — ValidationModules
Generated 2026-08-21 by `git diff` in a clone of github.com/ipjohnson/ValidationModules
at 5daa26c (Merge pull request #8), and verified with `git apply --check`
against a pristine clone of the same commit.

Measured against CSharpAuthor `feature/v2` at 4c7dc35.

This repository needs NO source change. The version bump below is the whole of its
migration, and this patch contains nothing else.

Measured, 8 test assemblies:
  1.1.1010 baseline   1,092 passed / 0 failed
  2.0                 1,092 passed / 0 failed — identical, unpatched

ValidationModules names no CSharpAuthor type anywhere in src/, tests/ or integ-tests/.
Its emitters build output with a StringBuilder and write their own `using global::`
lines. It sets PackageCSharpAuthorIncludeSource only to satisfy the 63 DependencyModules
generator-internal sources it imports from that package — which contain no [Generator]
and are never called from here. Those unmodified 1.x files compile against 2.0 with zero
errors.

NOTE ON THE VERSION LINE. The <PackageReference> bump to 2.0.0 is included because
it is part of the migration, but CSharpAuthor 2.0.0 is not published yet, so a
`dotnet restore` after applying this will fail with NU1102. To exercise the patch
today, apply it, put the version line back, and point the build at a 2.0 checkout —
see docs/migration-v1-v2.md section 9.2. Every measurement quoted above was taken
that way, with the wiring proved on each run.

diff --git a/src/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl.csproj b/src/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl.csproj
index 6cef964..3b5303f 100644
--- a/src/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl.csproj
+++ b/src/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/ValidationModules.SourceGenerator.Impl.csproj
@@ -80,13 +80,20 @@
             <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
         </PackageReference>
         <!--
-            1.1.1010 rather than 1.1.1007 because DependencyModules 1.0.0's InterceptorFileWriter
-            uses CSharpAuthor's ConstraintDefinition, which 1.1.1010 introduced. DM does not declare
-            a CSharpAuthor dependency - both are source-only packages compiled in side by side, so
-            the version that satisfies DM's sources is this project's problem to get right, and
-            nothing in the restore graph will raise it for us.
+            CSharpAuthor is compiled in only to satisfy the DependencyModules generator internals
+            imported above; nothing in this repository names a CSharpAuthor type. DM does not
+            declare a CSharpAuthor dependency - both are source-only packages compiled in side by
+            side, so the version that satisfies DM's sources is this project's problem to get
+            right, and nothing in the restore graph will raise it for us. 1.1.1010 rather than
+            1.1.1007 was because DependencyModules 1.0.0's InterceptorFileWriter uses
+            ConstraintDefinition, which 1.1.1010 introduced.
+
+            2.0.0 compiles those same DM sources unchanged - verified against a 2.0 checkout,
+            8 assemblies, 1,092 tests, 0 failures, byte-identical to the 1.1.1010 baseline.
+            2.0 removes only IOutputContext's two ITypeDefinition overloads of
+            AddImportNamespace/AddImportNamespaces, which DM's sources never call.
         -->
-        <PackageReference Include="CSharpAuthor" Version="1.1.1010">
+        <PackageReference Include="CSharpAuthor" Version="2.0.0">
             <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
             <IncludeAssets>build</IncludeAssets>
         </PackageReference>
